animous rule does not apply. The shape is `direction-only`.\n- **H.R. 82 bill text on congress.gov:** this is the same record as the roll call. I used the section repealing the government pension offset as `provision_quote`. The Act raises benefits for one group and has no tax side, so it meets only one clause of rung 2, which is compound. That matches codebook entry H5.\n- **Her own-site press release on the One Big Beautiful Bill:** these are her own words, coded `statement-other`. Her line \"tax relief for seniors on Social Security\" is about income tax on benefits, and the annex puts that next to the question rather than on it, so I coded it `adjacent`. The quote is marked not quotable (`not-forward`, `off-question`).\n\n`needs_source`: her own words or record on the payroll tax or the taxable maximum.\n\nSeveral connectors need authorizing before they can be used: Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Harvey and WorkOS, all through claude.ai connector settings. The GitHub plugin server failed to connect with an authorization-header error. This task needed none of them.","ttft_ms":9737,"type":"result","duration_ms":29012,"uuid":"23826de3-9246-4510-be3c-a56ae4730883","ttft_stream_ms":1763,"time_to_request_ms":72,"first_content_frame_ms":1763,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
